    "result_text": "All green. The full build compiles the openapi-generated `OwnerDto` (now with the integer `membershipLevel`) and the one acceptance test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), computed at creation.\n\n**Scoring rule:** start at 1; +1 when an email is present; +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`; capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` string property on the `Owner` schema with `membershipLevel` (integer, `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`, readOnly). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new field and drops the old one from the response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/MembershipLevel.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-source-of-truth helper `MembershipLevel.of(Owner)` implementing the additive scoring, mirroring the existing `Locality` helper pattern (kept off the mapper interface so MapStruct doesn't treat it as an implicit mapping method).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE `@Mapping` expression now targets `membershipLevel` via `MembershipLevel.of(owner)`.\n\n4. **`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/LogOwnerAudit.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=` instead of relying on the removed tier, using the same helper so it can't drift from the response value.\n\n5. **`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/CountHouseholdMembers.java`** \u2014 updated the stale javadoc that described the old GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE tier derivation (household size no longer feeds membership level).\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The audit log line confirms the new value: `AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 ... membershipLevel=3`.\n\nNote: the household-size count is still computed and exposed as its own `householdSize`/household field \u2014 I left that logic intact since it no longer affects the level but is independent data.",
